    {
      "title": "Varun Beverages Q3 results: Profit rises 13.5% to ₹830.6 cr, revenue up 33%",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/varun-beverages-q3-results-profit-rises-13-5-to-830-6-cr-revenue-up-33-126103000724_1.html",
      "description": "Varun Beverages Ltd, PepsiCo's largest franchise bottler, on Friday reported a 13.54 per cent on-year increase in consolidated net profit at Rs 830.6 crore for the September quarter of 2026, driven by double-digit volume growth in India and international markets.\nThe company, which follows the calendar year as its financial year, had posted a net profit of Rs 731.51 crore in the July-September quarter a year ago, according to a regulatory filing from Varun Beverages Ltd (VBL).\nRevenue from operations was up 33.3 per cent to Rs 6,815.58 crore in the September quarter of 2026. It stood at Rs 5,112.43 crore in the corresponding quarter of the last year.\nTotal expenses of VBL were up 35.77 per cent to Rs 5,880.55 crore in the September quarter.\nVBL's total consolidated income, which includes other income, in the September quarter was at Rs 6,935.44 crore, up 31.85 per cent.\nOn a standalone basis, which primarily includes India sales, VBL's revenue from operations was up 24.75 per cent",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-30T08:39:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Smartworks Q2 results: Net profit at ₹26 cr, revenue rises 37% to ₹605 cr",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/smartworks-q2-results-net-profit-at-26-cr-revenue-rises-37-to-605-cr-126103000597_1.html",
      "description": "Smartworks Coworking Spaces on Friday reported a consolidated net profit of Rs 25.64 crore for the quarter ended September on higher income.\nThe company had posted a net loss of Rs 3.13 crore in the year-ago period.\nTotal income rose 37 per cent to Rs 605.3 crore in the second quarter of this fiscal from Rs 441.06 crore in the corresponding period of the preceding year, according to a regulatory filing.\nSmartworks, which is one of the leading managed office space providers in the country, has a portfolio of 17.5 million sq ft across 71 centres in 15 cities across India and Singapore.\nNeetish Sarda, Founder & Managing Director, Smartworks, said: \"We have delivered a strong performance in the first half and are tracking well ahead of the plan we set for FY27.\"\n\"We are seeing sustained demand translate into growth. Existing clients are expanding with us across cities, while new global businesses, Indian conglomerates and GCCs are choosing our platform for their infrastructure needs.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-30T07:25:09"
    },
